  "findings": "Compared the Paul Lane spring frond photograph with all current three-size pilots and 36 variants. Uses undivided curved strap fronds rising from a basal crown, not pinnate male-fern leaves. Widened the blade envelope after the first pilot looked grass-like. Current variants span 0.23-0.47 m and include upright and arching fans. Curled tips, sori and fine undulating margins remain below 25 mm detail; emerging tips are represented by shorter fronds. Accepted as a stylized spring harts-tongue source, pending user variant endorsement.",
